          "Fingerprint": "sha256:6de3ef0442e4764f5d85bb9b00ecc35ccd97438f0f288bd21fbdc68cf59a7759",
          "Title": "msgpack: msgpack: Denial of Service via memory leak during map deserialization",
          "Description": "MessagePack is the serializer implementation for Python msgpack.org. Prior to 1.2.3, the msgpack-python C extension (msgpack._cmsgpack) leaks a decoded map value when deserialization rejects a key with strict_map_key=True (the default). Repeated malformed inputs can cause unbounded process memory growth and denial of service in applications that deserialize attacker-controlled MessagePack data. Both unpackb() and the streaming Unpacker API are affected. The pure-Python fallback does not exhibit this leak in the reported tests. This issue is fixed in version 1.2.3.",
